(Stage 1e3 - `is nothing` is the equality route (like `is true` / `is
 false`), NOT a type predicate. Critical correctness: `0 is nothing` MUST
 be false, because a nothing payload is 0 and a bare numeric compare
 would wrongly match. `nothing is nothing` is true. A `value` carrying
 nothing (passed as an argument) is nothing. Acceptance: the four lines.)

if nothing is nothing, print "nothing is nothing".
if 0 is nothing, print "0 is nothing (BUG)".
if 0 is not nothing, print "0 is not nothing".

To check with a value called v.
  if v is nothing, print "v is nothing".

check of nothing.